WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.513 --> 00:00:03.292
(blast off and sonic boom)

00:00:03.292 --> 00:00:05.792
(piano music)

00:00:15.930 --> 00:00:18.739
- [Evan] My founding story.

00:00:18.739 --> 00:00:21.438
If you can shape your business
life or your working life,

00:00:21.438 --> 00:00:23.940
you can just look at it
at as another extension,

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:26.611
you just fulfill all your
values as a human being

00:00:26.611 --> 00:00:27.828
in the workplace.

00:00:27.828 --> 00:00:29.645
If you're an activist,
you bring the activism

00:00:29.645 --> 00:00:31.566
of your life into your business,

00:00:31.566 --> 00:00:34.704
or if you love creative
art, you can bring that in.

00:00:34.704 --> 00:00:36.597
Anita Roddick, founder of The Body Shop

00:00:36.597 --> 00:00:39.888
and pioneer of ethical consumerism.

00:00:39.888 --> 00:00:41.676
I never wanted to tell my story.

00:00:41.676 --> 00:00:44.650
When I started my website I
wanted to build a great resource

00:00:44.650 --> 00:00:47.131
to help entrepreneurs succeed.

00:00:47.131 --> 00:00:49.009
I started with stories
of famous entrepreneurs

00:00:49.009 --> 00:00:51.658
like Bill Gates, Oprah
Winfrey, and Walt Disney,

00:00:51.658 --> 00:00:54.743
because their stories inspired me.

00:00:54.743 --> 00:00:56.827
When I was down, when I doubted myself,

00:00:56.827 --> 00:00:58.780
when I felt like I
wasn't going to make it,

00:00:58.780 --> 00:01:00.192
I looked to their stories

00:01:00.192 --> 00:01:03.424
and they motivated me to keep going.

00:01:03.424 --> 00:01:05.404
Bill Gates' story saved my business

00:01:05.404 --> 00:01:08.201
and made me stick with
being an entrepreneur.

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.967
I wanted to share that
knowledge with others

00:01:09.967 --> 00:01:11.345
so they could also be motivated

00:01:11.345 --> 00:01:14.160
to continue to pursue their dreams.

00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:15.362
I created an awesome website,

00:01:15.362 --> 00:01:17.144
but people kept writing in saying,

00:01:17.144 --> 00:01:20.988
love the site, but who is Evan Carmichael?

00:01:20.988 --> 00:01:23.365
I'm nobody compared to the
entrepreneurs I'm profiling

00:01:23.365 --> 00:01:27.077
I thought, but people were
asking so I started to share,

00:01:27.077 --> 00:01:29.741
and my business took off.

00:01:29.741 --> 00:01:31.512
Suddenly I was attracting more clients,

00:01:31.512 --> 00:01:34.150
more website traffic, more
social media followers.

00:01:34.150 --> 00:01:35.156
I was selling more products,

00:01:35.156 --> 00:01:36.586
getting more newsletter signups,

00:01:36.586 --> 00:01:39.010
receiving more media
requests for interviews.

00:01:39.010 --> 00:01:41.177
I was having more fun too.

00:01:43.006 --> 00:01:44.566
The product I had was already great,

00:01:44.566 --> 00:01:47.819
but when I told my story,
it added more context,

00:01:47.819 --> 00:01:51.700
it made it feel more valuable,
it connected with people.

00:01:51.700 --> 00:01:54.192
When I talk about how I was
making 300 dollars a month

00:01:54.192 --> 00:01:57.534
in my first business, and Bill
Gate's story saved my company

00:01:57.534 --> 00:02:00.079
and helped me build an
international business

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:02.463
and get acquired just a
couple of years later,

00:02:02.463 --> 00:02:04.281
that adds context.

00:02:04.281 --> 00:02:07.462
People really want to
hear what I have to say.

00:02:07.462 --> 00:02:08.822
I realized that telling my story

00:02:08.822 --> 00:02:11.309
wasn't about pumping myself up.

00:02:11.309 --> 00:02:14.153
It humanized my business and
made it easier for people

00:02:14.153 --> 00:02:17.633
to take whatever next step
I was asking them to take.

00:02:17.633 --> 00:02:20.285
It's time for you to write your story.

00:02:20.285 --> 00:02:22.868
(upbeat music)

00:02:38.325 --> 00:02:40.725
(blast off and sonic boom)

